# ======================================================================
# EDIT 1 — ADD this node to section 4 ("The negative control"), after
#          [CXC-BPO-NEGATIVE-CONTROL].
# ======================================================================

### [CXC-BPO-BOARD-QA-NOT-LAND-GATE] The board-derived checks are BOARD-QA — outside the composeio LAND GATE
- definition: every check whose outcome is a function of a fabricated `.kicad_pcb` that lives OUTSIDE this repo (David's `pcb/` tree — the geometry-coincidence cross-check, the rail-classification sweep, and every negative control that derives from a live board) is BOARD-QA. It is SKIPPED in the default land-gate invocation and runs only under `COMPOSEIO_BOARD_QA=1` (marker `board_qa`, seam `tests/_hermetic_policy.py`, the dual of the glass policy's `needs_glass`).
- premise: a land gate exists to catch what a DELTA broke. A test whose result depends on state no delta controls — an out-of-repo file that David may bodge or respin at will — is not a delta-regression check; it is a property of the environment it happened to read. Routing it through the gate makes a green land hostage to a working tree the committer does not own.
- ruling: David, 2026-08-28 — "the lego_dots board is already fabricated; it is what it is. Its geometry is MY concern. It must NOT block composeio code lands." A fabricated board changing is a BOARD finding, delivered to the bench, never a code-land blocker.
- boundary: this SCOPES the board checks out of the gate; it does NOT delete them. `COMPOSEIO_BOARD_QA=1 pytest tests -m board_qa` still fires the full negative-control battery — the instrument that proves the deriver READS the board is preserved, exactly as `[CXC-BPO-NEGATIVE-CONTROL]` requires; it is only relocated off the land path.
- generalisation: the same shape as the glass policy ([PRINCIPLE-MACHINE-GREEN-IS-NOT-GLASS-GREEN]) and the away-watch guard — a check whose truth lives in ONE invocation path is a property of that path. Lift the "reads out-of-repo state" property to the seam every pytest crosses (`tests/conftest.py`) so no future board-reading test can silently re-arm the gate; a test that requests an out-of-repo board fixture is `board_qa` by construction (auto-marked).
- enforced-by: `tests/test_land_gate_is_hermetic.py` — fails if the geometry check is not `board_qa`, if the default land-gate invocation still selects it, or if a default run of the beep-out module is not green.
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-BPO]

