# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# REPLACE WITH:
- cross-check: the netlist reader carries an INDEPENDENT internal check — pad positions agree with the copper endpoints written by a DIFFERENT code path in the same file (`board.geometry_coincidence()`). Two writers of one file agreeing is evidence the reader is reading, not guessing. ⛔ This coincidence is a property of the LIVE fabricated board, not of the parser: a clean design meets a high bar (the gauge and button boards do), a respun or bodged board may not (`lego_dots` fell from 92/92 to 94/121 after a respin — a BOARD finding, David's to resolve). The check therefore belongs to BOARD-QA, not the land gate ([CXC-BPO-BOARD-QA-NOT-LAND-GATE]); its assertion is that a GOOD board's copper coincides with the parsed geometry, run under `COMPOSEIO_BOARD_QA=1`.

